        "original_id": "43213145-2e89-5508-b9e4-21432af47388",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Roger Donaldson, André Cayatte, Chris Donaldson\n- Films: The World's Fastest Indian, Smash Palace, No Way Out, Thirteen Days, Dante's Peak, Black Dossier\n- Roles: film director, producer, writer, filmmaker, lawyer\n- Topics: crime, justice, moral responsibility, family relationship\n\nFacts:\n- André Cayatte was born on 3 February 1909 in Carcassonne and died on 6 February 1989 in Paris.\n- André Cayatte was a French filmmaker and lawyer known for films about crime, justice, and moral responsibility.\n- Black Dossier is a 1955 French drama film directed by André Cayatte.\n- Roger Donaldson was born on 15 November 1945 and is an Australian-born New Zealand film director, producer, and writer.\n- Roger Donaldson directed films including Smash Palace, The World's Fastest Indian, No Way Out, Thirteen Days, and Dante's Peak.\n- Chris Donaldson is the son of film director Roger Donaldson.",
